arm64: state required Harmony clock contract

The shipped arm64 kernel runs only inside Harmony and its image build requires
the paravirtual clock. Remove Kconfig help that suggests ordinary Linux boot is
a supported mode. The registration path already stops on a missing or
incompatible host interface.

This patch is Linux-kernel code (GPL-2.0), carried as a diff under the Harmony
repository's designated guest-kernel patch exception.

--- a/drivers/clocksource/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/Kconfig
@@ -337,7 +337,7 @@
 	  access and the vDSO fast path are disabled; no live-counter fallback
 	  exists because reachable Neoverse N1 hardware cannot trap CNTVCT.
 
-	  This is a dedicated Harmony guest option. Say N for ordinary kernels.
+	  The shipped Harmony guest requires this interface at boot.
 
 config HARMONY_ARM_USER_COUNTER_TRAPS
 	bool "Harmony deny EL0 generic-counter reads"
